    "summary": "Rewrote the wfmt container implementation to match the authoritative samples in assets/ rather than the superseded docs/FORMAT.md draft.\n\nFormat recovered from the samples (hand-decoded both files byte by byte):\n- Header, 9 bytes: magic `WFMT`, version 1, then record count as **little-endian** u32 (sample.wfmt has `05 00 00 00`; the draft said big-endian).\n- Record: `uvarint tag` + `uvarint length` + payload, then the record's total size is zero-padded up to a multiple of 4. Padding is excluded from `length` but included in the checksum. This is what the draft omitted entirely.\n- Trailer: standard CRC-32 (zlib/PKZIP: poly 0xEDB88320, init 0xFFFFFFFF, **with** the final XOR the draft said to skip), little-endian, over every preceding byte.\n\nI verified sample.wfmt decodes to exactly 5 records — (1, b\"alpha\"), (2, b\"\"), (300, b\"x\"*10), (4, bytes(range(256))), (70000, b\"z\") — re-encoding to the original 309 bytes, and hand-computed the empty sample's CRC as 0x906B8493, matching its stored ",
